<ul class="features-list"><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Rage &amp; Legit aim</li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Player ESP &amp; chams</li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Class &amp; weapon skins</li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Movement &amp; view controls</li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>Lua &amp; saved profiles</li></ul></div></aside></div>
<div class="description-section" id="product-details"><div class="product-section-heading"><div><span class="product-eyebrow">MAKE IT YOURS</span><h2 class="section-title">Your class. Your setup.</h2></div><a href="/features-list/tf2-features/">View all features →</a></div>
<div class="description-content"><p>Scooby brings the original Team Fortress 2 and TF2 Classified into one loader entry, with a separate package and profile for each edition. Start with the shared tools, then explore the controls built for your game.</p>
<div class="gmod-feature-grid product-feature-grid"><section><h3>Rage &amp; Legit</h3><p>Use independent aim and trigger profiles, Camera or Silent aim, target filters, smoothing, FOV and activation keys.</p></section><section><h3>Player &amp; world ESP</h3><p>Tune player boxes, skeletons, health, names and distance. Give teammates, buildings, health packs, ammo and dropped weapons their own settings.</p></section><section><h3>Independent chams</h3><p>Style players, teammates, self, arms, weapons, buildings and items. Visible, invisible and overlay passes have separate colors, materials and animations.</p></section><section><h3>Class &amp; weapon skins</h3><p>Browse the installed class and weapon catalog, preview appearances and select supported model skin families. Skin choices are local visual changes.</p></section><section><h3>Movement &amp; view</h3><p>Configure bunny hop, auto strafe, camera FOV and model FOV. Retail also exposes viewmodel position and angle offsets.</p></section><section><h3>World &amp; game modes</h3><p>Retail includes separate objective and mode-object visuals plus MvM controls. Classified provides its own building, projectile, objective and NPC visuals.</p></section><section><h3>Lua scripting</h3><p>Use the built-in editor, script manager and console. Read player snapshots, draw overlays and add custom controls through the TF2 API.</p></section><section><h3>Profiles &amp; interface</h3><p>Save settings, assign hotkeys, search features, manage Favorites and adjust the interface and overlay scales.</p></section></div>
<section class="gmod-setup" id="setup"><h3>Get started with TF2</h3><ol><li>Sign in to Scooby and open TF2.</li><li>Choose Team Fortress 2 or TF2 Classified. The dashboard dropdown lets you switch later.</li><li>Follow the <a href="/guides/tf2/getting-started/">setup guide</a>, load the matching package and open a local practice session.</li><li>Press Insert or F1, then choose your settings or load a saved profile.</li></ol><p>The TF2 family is a preview. Edition-specific settings and game-update compatibility are described in the <a href="/guides/tf2/">wiki</a> and <a href="/features-list/tf2-features/">feature library</a>.</p></section>
<section class="gmod-faq" aria-labelledby="tf2-faq-title"><h3 id="tf2-faq-title">Common questions</h3><details><summary>Is TF2 free?</summary><p>Yes. Both retail TF2 and TF2 Classified are free for signed-in Scooby users. No separate TF2 purchase is required.</p></details><details><summary>Does this include TF2 Classified?</summary><p>Yes. Choose Team Fortress 2 or TF2 Classified in the loader popup or dashboard dropdown. Each edition keeps its own game files, settings and scripts.</p></details><details><summary>Are the screenshots taken in game?</summary><p>The three Classified screenshots are actual captures from a local Hydro session. The two retail images are labeled interface previews from the standalone preview application.</p></details><details><summary>Which features work in both editions?</summary><p>The core combat, player visuals, chams, skins, movement and scripting pages are shared. Mode-specific controls differ; the <a href="/features-list/tf2-features/">full feature list</a> marks the edition-specific options.</p></details><details><summary>How do I get started?</summary><p>Open TF2 in the loader, choose your edition and follow the <a href="/guides/tf2/getting-started/">setup guide</a>. Use Insert or F1 to open the interface after loading. The current preview supports eligible local practice sessions.</p></details><details><summary>Can I add my own Lua scripts?</summary><p>Yes. Start with the <a href="/docs/tf2/">downloadable examples</a>, then use the <a href="/api/tf2/">TF2 API reference</a> for functions, settings and shared UI controls.</p></details></section></div></div></main><div class="lightbox" id="lightbox" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="TF2 screenshot gallery" aria-hidden="true"><button type="button" class="lightbox-close" aria-label="Close preview">×</button><button type="button" class="lightbox-nav lightbox-prev" aria-label="Previous preview">‹</button><figure><img id="lightbox-img" alt=""><figcaption id="lightbox-caption"></figcaption></figure><button type="button" class="lightbox-nav lightbox-next" aria-label="Next preview">›</button></div><footer class="footer">
